{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals","id":1041160,"title":"Historical Ministries of the Iron Seals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T02:43:05-08:00","id":1041160,"title":"Historical Ministries of the Iron Seals","content":"According to Seer doctrine, there have always been four Great Ministries, and four Archigenitors amongst the ten (or ten-and-one) Iron Seal Exarchs. The current four have also &quot;always&quot; been the true Archigenitors, even if &quot;imperfect&quot; records hold that this was not the case.<br /> <br /> For the Greater Ministries<br /> The Hegemonic Ministry (the Unity) was formalised in 1500.<br /> The Ministry of the Paternoster (the Father) was founded after the Fourth Crusade and rose to prominence in the 13th century.<br /> The Praetorian Ministry (the General) emerged from and supplanted their Diadochi predecessors in the 1st century BC to 3rd century AD.<br /> The Ministry of Panopticon (the Eye) formed in the 18th century, and rose to prominence after WW2, and solidified its status when the Cold War was at its height.<br /> <br /> For the Lesser Ministries<br /> The Mammonic MInistry (the Chancellor) are on the rise after WW2, but are still the largest of the Lesser Ministries<br /> The Pantechnicon Ministry (also the Chancellor) came together over the 19th century, but lost out to the Panopticon for the top four.<br /> The Secret Order of the Gate (the Gate) dates back to 1901, and has always been a demi-Ministry.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I'm left wondering in the specific: whose place was being fought over between the Pantechnicon and the Panopticon, or is the idea that there have always been four Archigenitors a lie to try and look more important?<br /> <br /> More generally, do we have anything on the other Cults and Ministries after Alexander's time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:29:13-08:00","id":1041172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals#post1041160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mammonic MInistry (the Chancellor) are on the rise after WW2, but are still the largest of the Lesser Ministries<br /> The Pantechnicon Ministry (also the Chancellor) came together over the 19th century, but lost out to the Panopticon for the top four.<br /> The Secret Order of the Gate (the Gate) dates back to 1901, and has always been a demi-Ministry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure about those? Mammonic Ministry sounds as being connected strictly to rise of XVIII century capitalism - it's just get suppressed by Panopticon for Archigenitor title. Pantechnicon <i>are</i> remnants of Nameless War od 19th century. And I'm almost sure Secret Order of the Gate is as old as Seers of Throne as Order itself, i.e. early Roman Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T04:54:42-08:00","id":1041199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals#post1041160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm left wondering in the specific: whose place was being fought over between the Pantechnicon and the Panopticon, or is the idea that there have always been four Archigenitors a lie to try and look more important?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fairly plausible. At the very least, I don't remember reading anything about a fallen ministry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T05:08:19-08:00","id":1041203,"title":"","content":"I'd say that within the setting, the Seers lie to themselves just as much as they spread misinformation to those of other loyalties. So, even within the Seers book, some of the material is probably misinformation that the current Seers believe, but might not be literally true since the Exarchs do have the ability, at least collectively, to alter the very foundations of reality and rewrite time so that certain cities/cultures never existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:08:32-08:00","id":1041261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals?p=1041172#post1041172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure about those? Mammonic Ministry sounds as being connected strictly to rise of XVIII century capitalism - it's just get suppressed by Panopticon for Archigenitor title. Pantechnicon <i>are</i> remnants of Nameless War od 19th century. And I'm almost sure Secret Order of the Gate is as old as Seers of Throne as Order itself, i.e. early Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Secret Order's founding is in the Legacy writeup, with 1901 being the date when the three founders apparently found the Gate in chicago. At least, this is the current version of the legacy/ministry/cult.<br /> <br /> The Hegemonic Ministry's teetering on the edge wasn't until its loss of prestige after WW2. There's nothing on when they were founded, but all of the materials in Mage Noir talks about the competition at the time being between the Pantechnicon and Panopticon in the early post-war period. It seems that Mammon only became dominant fairly recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:38:54-08:00","id":1041284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals?p=1041261#post1041261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Secret Order's founding is in the Legacy writeup, with 1901 being the date when the three founders apparently found the Gate in chicago. At least, this is the current version of the legacy/ministry/cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacy interation maybe is only from start of XX century - but even <b>DaveB</b> mentioned that how Seers are setup makes higher numbers in them as Scelesti - Abyss Worshippers are just punish even more sever than in Pentacle. To me, Order of Gate as cult/Legacy/Methodology just comes again and again in Seers dogma, reinventing itself few decades after last. This from 1901 is probably the newest reincarnation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals?p=1041261#post1041261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hegemonic Ministry's teetering on the edge wasn't until its loss of prestige after WW2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hegemony are from year 1600, it's in their write-up. From then on they are first Archigenitor as they are first true Ministry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals?p=1041261#post1041261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing on when they were founded, but all of the materials in Mage Noir talks about the competition at the time being between the Pantechnicon and Panopticon in the early post-war period.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's logical in 'nuclear war fear' and 'Cold War of Intelligence' era to have those to fight for title of Archigenitor. Only recent showing of surveillance pointed that Panopticon is one that won.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041160-historical-ministries-of-the-iron-seals?p=1041261#post1041261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that Mammon only became dominant fairly recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Mammon recently fight for title of Archigenitor is not precluding it for existing for centuries. For example, I imagine Mammonist to be largest supporters of slave trade in Enlightenment and <a href=\"http://vichist.blogspot.com/2010/03/child-labour-in-victorian-england.html\" target=\"_blank\">child labour in Victorian</a> era. Whenever post Ministry reform of 1600 people treated others as items to be exploit for their profit - Mammon Seers were sustaining this society structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-31-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}